Binary image: the white areas are copper and the black areas are substrate. There are small features: a tiny black speck inside the copper near (372,117), which looks like a pinhole. A small white blob at (403,314) on the substrate is a stray copper spot. A few small spurs sit on the copper edges at (235,233), (530,360) and (225,390).

The worst defect is the isolated copper spot at (403,314), which is a "copper" defect (spurious copper). It is small and isolated, so it is not a short. Copper ranks above spur and pinhole, so that is the one to report. Disposition is rework, with minor severity.

